# headon-attack: two bodies of one footprint head on in a lane one body wide, one of them on an attack or guard leg.
#   lane 1  X1 on a move order east, Y1 on an attack order on an enemy body beyond the lane's west end
#   lane 2  X2 on a move order east, Y2 on a guard order on a body of its own beyond the west end
#   lane 3  X3 on an attack-move order east, Y3 on an attack order (as lane 1)
# A known limit, not a fix: all three pairs stand for good, as before the rules for bodies that stand for good. The
# swap and the give-way in a knot serve legs that complete at a point; a body on an attack or guard leg is its
# owner's to end, is never moved by those rules and reads as live (the bodies behind a firing line must keep their
# orders, siege-gap.scn), so the body it blocks is never dead either and neither gives way nor ends its order
# (docs/legion-pathfinding.md, "Known weaknesses"). headon-fight.scn is the same meet on two attack-move orders,
# which the late swap resolves.
# Keys: g.X1.complete_n, g.X2.complete_n, g.X3.complete_n (0 each), open_still900 (6).
scn 1
name headon-attack
ticks 12000
seed 7
players 2
team 0 0
team 1 1
wanderers off
map flat 96 64
wall 16 0 64 10
wall 16 12 64 10
wall 16 24 64 10
wall 16 36 64 28
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
type g mover 2 2500 10 1.79999 gun=40,1,1.0
type tgt mover 2 2500 10 1.8 hp=30000
group X1 0 m 1 cells 6,10
group Y1 0 g 1 cells 86,10 weapons=on
group T1 1 tgt 1 cells 2,10 weapons=off
group X2 0 m 1 cells 6,22
group Y2 0 m 1 cells 86,22
group W2 0 m 1 cells 2,22
group X3 0 m 1 cells 6,34
group Y3 0 g 1 cells 86,34 weapons=on
group T3 1 tgt 1 cells 2,34 weapons=off
at 2 move X1 90 11
at 2 attack Y1 @T1
at 2 move X2 90 23
at 2 guard Y2 @W2
at 2 fight X3 90 35
at 2 attack Y3 @T3
